 include pension funds, insurers and mutual funds; leveraged funds are mainly hedge funds and trading advisers; small traders hold less than the CFTC's reporting size. Contracts of different futures are different sizes, so counts are compared within one book, never across books. Source: CFTC Commitments of Traders."}